{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And overtake you.</b> Written plene with a ו״ו, whereas in the blessings it is not written plene; and the reason it is written here plene is on account of what is said (Psalms 91:15): ״עמו אנכי בצרה״ — 'I am with him in distress' — and this is likewise hinted in this verse in the final letters of the words. And because the Torah frightens them with the curses, it comes to hint that they will not perish in them, for the hidden Name, dwelling within them, is present in their distress and guards them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:33.939656882Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}